    "body": "## Summary\n- reject attempts to bookmark the caller's own job\n- remove the current user's stale bookmarks before returning the saved-jobs shortlist\n- keep existing idempotent save/remove and batch status behavior unchanged\n- document saved-job ownership and lifecycle cleanup\n\n## Why\nSaved jobs are meant to be a private shortlist of actionable opportunities. Own-job bookmarks are meaningless, and accepted/completed/cancelled jobs should not accumulate as hidden stale rows after they leave the public `OPEN` market.\n\n## Safety / architecture\n- no new public data exposure or exact-location access\n- cleanup is scoped strictly to the authenticated user's bookmarks\n- no schema change is required; the existing saved-job indexes and foreign keys remain the persistence boundary\n\n## Validation\n- unit coverage for own-job rejection and stale-bookmark cleanup\n- run full Maven verify, frontend lint/build, Flyway/PostgreSQL smokes and existing runtime/payment gates\n- do not merge unless required checks are green",
